For newly developed measuring methods, ZIF-8 is utilized for the study of self-assembly mechanism, interfacial structures, and surface termination modes of MOFs, COFs, and zeolites. Paving the way for HRTEM imaging on materials like MOFs, zeolites, polymers, covalent organic frameworks, and two-dimensional materials.[94]
## 3. Conclusions and Outlook
In numerous experimental cases, ZIF-8 has served as the prior representative to demonstrate the result. Recently, a great number of remarkable breakthroughs in the improvement of the applications of porous materials such as catalysis, adsorption, electrochemistry, and so on have been demonstrated with the attendance of ZIF-8. Though many other materials can more or less accomplish some of the leading functions of ZIF-8, they are not as cost-effective, stable, or producible. Starting from ZIF-8, we can get unbelievably abundant sorts of materials with unlimited potentials and usages. Not only purephased microporous ZIF-8 can play as an outstanding catalyst and adsorbent, its porosity, morphology, and topology can be facilely adjusted through different processes. Tailoring nanoarchitectures for functional applications of ZIF-8 is also promising for its high-density active sites and open windows.[95] Encapsulation of various nanoparticles for different catalytic systems is also astonishing available for photocatalysts, electrocatalysts, capacitors, and electrodes when the host framework is ZIF-8. ZIF-8-contained composites and ZIF-8-derived materials can also lead to a wide range of functional materials that serve different purposes.[18] In addition, ZIF-8 is the most commonly commercialized MOF that is of low cost and high productivity and performance, based on which it is doubtless to say that ZIF-8 will continue to be the most successful commercialized MOF for a considerably long period. Also, it is of high promise that products derived from ZIF-8 will also meet their market sometime in the future. In conclusion, we can put it this way that the discovery and utilizations of ZIF-8 has largely boosted the research development of MOFs and other porous materials, understanding the importance and utilization of this zeolitic imidazolate framework is remarkably essential for future research of all porous materials, and it would be of broad interest to further understand whether ZIF-8 is popular only due to its very easy chemistry compared to other MOFs or just because of its intrinsic properties.
